      "name": "InitStringTables",
      "signature": "int InitStringTables(int fLoadExpansion, char * szLocalePath)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes the game's string tables for localization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If already initialized (g_pStringTable != NULL), increment ref count and return\n2. Determine locale path (use szPath if provided, else get from registry)\n3. Detect character set (CJK, Cyrillic, Latin2, Latin) based on locale\n4. Load font system map from data\\local\\font\\%s\\default.map\n5. Load main string table from data\\local\\lng\\%s\\string.tbl\n6. Allocate and populate string pointer array (g_ppwszStrings)\n7. Convert strings to Unicode (g_pwszStringData)\n8. Load patch string table (patchstring.tbl), allocate g_ppwszPatchStrings\n9. If fLoadExp, load expansion string table (expansionstring.tbl)\n10. Initialize number formatting suffixes (K=Kilo, M=Million, B=Billion, T=Trillion)\n\nParameters:\n- fLoadExp (int): If non-zero, load expansion string table\n- szPath (char*): Locale path override (NULL to use registry)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success\n- 0 if main string table fails to load\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x11 (17): String entry stride in table\n- 0x15 (21): Header size before string entries\n- 0x14d0-0x14d3: String IDs for K/M/B/T suffixes\n- 0x3fffffff: Mask for hash count (30-bit value)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
