      "signature": "void ComputeCrc16(byte * pData, ushort * pwCrcOut, uint dwIndexStart, uint dwIndexEnd)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Computes CRC16 checksum over a byte range using lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwIndexStart < dwIndexEnd (asserts on failure)\n2. Initialize CRC to 0xFFFF\n3. For each byte from dwIndexStart to dwIndexEnd-1:\n   - XOR high byte of CRC with current byte to get table index\n   - Shift CRC left 8 bits and XOR with table entry\n4. Store final CRC16 at pwCrcOut\n\nParameters:\n- pData (byte*): Source data buffer\n- pwCrcOut (ushort*): Output pointer for CRC16 result\n- dwIndexStart (uint): Starting byte index (inclusive)\n- dwIndexEnd (uint): Ending byte index (exclusive)\n\nReturns:\n- void (result stored via pwCrcOut)\n\nNotes:\n- Uses g_awCrc16Table (256-entry lookup table at 0x6fc4d7e0)\n- CRC16-CCITT polynomial (standard table-driven implementation)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:3",
