      "name": "GetLanguageLocaleId",
      "signature": "uint GetLanguageLocaleId(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Returns the language locale ID, initializing from data file on first call.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if locale already initialized via g_fLocaleInitialized flag\n2. If not, load \"data\\\\local\\\\use\" file via FUN_6fc44882\n3. Read first byte as locale ID and store in g_dwLocaleId\n4. Validate locale ID is <= 12; reset to 0 if invalid\n5. Return cached g_dwLocaleId\n\nParameters:\n- (none)\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Locale ID (0-12), 0 if invalid or uninitialized\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x473 (1139): Source line number for file load\n- 0xC (12): Maximum valid locale ID\n- 6: Korean/CJK locale (special line-break rules in caller)",
