      "name": "Int64ToUnicodeWithSeparators",
      "signature": "void Int64ToUnicodeWithSeparators(uint dwLow, int nHigh, Unicode * pwszOutput, int nMaxLen)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts 64-bit signed integer to Unicode string with thousands separators.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer length >= 3, assert on failure\n2. If negative, write '-' prefix and negate the value\n3. Convert int64 to ASCII decimal via FUN_6fc44bbf\n4. Calculate output length including comma separators (len + (len-1)/3)\n5. Copy digits right-to-left, inserting ',' (0x2c) every 3 digits\n6. If length is 0, output \"0\" as fallback\n\nParameters:\n- dwLow (uint): Low 32 bits of the 64-bit integer\n- nHigh (int): High 32 bits (signed for negativity check)\n- pwszOutput (Unicode*): Destination buffer for formatted string\n- nMaxLen (int): Maximum characters in output buffer\n\nReturns:\n- void (result written to pwszOutput)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2d (45): Unicode minus sign '-'\n- 0x2c (44): Unicode comma ','\n- 10: Decimal radix for conversion\n- 3: Digits between thousand separators",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:47da28048f38b8cc4d19845db308498e",
