      "name": "FormatAbbreviatedNumber",
      "signature": "void FormatAbbreviatedNumber(int nHigh, int nLow, wchar_t * wszOut, int nOutLen)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Formats a 64-bit number with abbreviated magnitude suffixes and comma separators.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate output buffer length >= 3, assert on failure\n2. Convert 64-bit value (nHigh:nLow) to decimal string via FUN_6fc44c76\n3. Calculate string length and determine magnitude tier (0-4)\n4. Compute display digits and comma count for output length check\n5. Select suffix character: none(0), K(1), M(2), B(3), T(4)\n6. Write digits right-to-left with comma insertion every 3 digits\n7. On empty/overflow, fallback to \"0\" via Unicode conversion\n\nParameters:\n- nHigh (int): High 32 bits of 64-bit value\n- nLow (int): Low 32 bits of 64-bit value\n- wszOut (wchar_t*): Output buffer for formatted Unicode string\n- nOutLen (int): Output buffer length in characters\n\nReturns:\n- void (result written to wszOut)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x55555556: Division by 3 magic constant\n- 0x2c (44): ASCII comma character\n- 3: Digits between commas, digits per magnitude tier\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fc44c76: Int64 to decimal string conversion\n- Ordinal_10023: Assertion handler",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
