      "name": "BinarySearchArray",
      "signature": "uint BinarySearchArray(void * pContext, uint nLow, uint nCount, int nStride, void * pfnCompare)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Performs binary search on a strided array using a comparison callback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate high bound from count and stride\n2. Divide count in half and test midpoint via callback\n3. If callback returns 0, element found - return index\n4. If callback returns negative, search lower half\n5. If callback returns positive, search upper half\n6. Repeat until found or count exhausted\n\nParameters:\n- pContext (void*): Opaque context passed to comparison callback\n- nLow (uint): Starting array index (byte offset)\n- nCount (uint): Number of elements to search\n- nStride (int): Byte stride between elements\n- pfnCompare (void*): Callback(pContext, nIndex) returns 0=match, <0=go lower, >0=go higher\n\nReturns:\n- Element index on match, 0 if not found\n\nNotes:\n- Callback semantics: negative=target below, positive=target above\n- Returns 0 on failure (ambiguous if index 0 is valid target)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
