      "name": "InitializeCodePageLocale",
      "signature": "int InitializeCodePageLocale(int nLocaleId)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes the character type table (g_abCharTypeTable) for a given code page.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Lock CRT critical section 0x19\n2. Resolve locale ID to code page via FUN_6fc49735 (handles -2=OEM, -3=ACP, -4=default)\n3. If code page unchanged, return 0 (success)\n4. Search g_adwKnownCodePages for predefined code page entry\n5. If found, populate character type table from predefined ranges\n6. If not found, call GetCPInfo to get code page info\n7. For multi-byte code pages, mark lead bytes with 0x4 and all bytes 1-254 with 0x8\n8. Store code page LCID via FUN_6fc4977f (maps 932->0x411, 936->0x804, etc.)\n9. Unlock critical section and return status\n\nParameters:\n- nLocaleId (int): Locale/code page ID (-2=OEM, -3=ACP, -4=default, or direct CP value)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success\n- -1 on failure (GetCPInfo failed and no fallback allowed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x19: CRT critical section ID for locale\n- 0x30 (48): Stride of predefined code page entry\n- 0x4: Lead byte flag in character type table\n- 0x8: Valid multi-byte char flag",
